{# repair_claim.j2 — Targeted claim repair prompt #}
{{ language_instruction }}

A claim has failed validation. Rewrite it to fix the specific issue.

FAILED CLAIM:
"{{ claim_text }}"

CITED FACTS (the ONLY permitted sources):
{% for fact in cited_facts %}
[{{ fact.fact_id }}] {{ fact.canonical_text }}
{% endfor %}

VALIDATION FAILURE:
Type: {{ failure_type }}
{% if offending_span %}
Offending span: "{{ offending_span }}" — this token is NOT grounded in the cited facts.
{% endif %}
{% if entailment_score %}
Entailment score: {{ entailment_score }} (below threshold {{ threshold }})
{% endif %}

REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS:
1. Remove or replace any token not directly supported by the cited facts.
2. Do NOT add information from outside the cited facts.
3. Maintain the same intent and section context.
4. Keep the rewritten claim concise.

Output JSON:
{
  "claim_id": "{{ claim_id }}",
  "text": "<rewritten claim text>",
  "fact_ids": {{ fact_ids | tojson }},
  "repair_note": "<brief explanation of what was changed>"
}
